    "evidence": "Across all evaluated sm_120 cohort cells the cache-op classifier maps ZERO loads to L1-eligible (.ca): total L1-eligible misses and L1 hits absorbed are both 0, so the per-SM L1 filter is inert. This is the DOCUMENTED conservative behavior of the arch-coupling discipline, not a defect: l1_cache_op_classifier._BARE_LDG_E_DEFAULTS_TO_CA admits only sm_86 (where bare LDG.E resolves to the ISA-default .CA), and every other arch -- sm_120 included -- keeps bare LDG.E -> OTHER (ineligible) 'until their default modifier is explicitly documented and tested'. The Blackwell loads observed (LDG.E.U16.CONSTANT, descriptor-based desc[UR..]) match the bare-LDG.E rule and route to OTHER -> bypass, or to the unmodeled-drop path (4 cells reach L2 with zero accesses -> a vacuous 0.0). The L1-miss-filtered L2 predictor therefore cannot be exercised as designed on sm_120, and the median absolute error stays far above the gate.",
    "promotion_trigger": "Add sm_120 to l1_cache_op_classifier._BARE_LDG_E_DEFAULTS_TO_CA (and model the .CONSTANT / descriptor-based / uniform-datapath load forms) with documented + tested Blackwell cache-op semantics, so sm_120 loads acquire .ca/.cg eligibility and the per-SM L1 filter is exercised; then re-run the L1-miss-filtered evaluation. The named family becomes load-bearing only if the median absolute error then clears the gate."
